---
name: Grounded QA
description: >
  Revision 2. A question answered against a supplied passage — the prompt this
  feature edits and re-scores, so that "the edit improved the answer" becomes a
  measurement rather than an impression (FR-006, SC-004).

  Revision 1 was deliberately bare: it asked for an answer and said nothing
  about staying inside the material. It scored groundedness 5.0 — the model
  stayed inside the passage without being told to. That is a genuine result and
  not the one the revision was written to expect, so the honest reading is that
  a single well-posed question against a short passage does not put much
  pressure on groundedness at all.

  The rule below is therefore an insurance policy rather than a fix: it makes
  staying inside the source a stated requirement instead of a lucky outcome,
  and it gives the model something to do — say so — when the passage does not
  cover what was asked, which revision 1 left undefined.
authors:
  - Valerio Quaranta
model:
  api: chat
  configuration:
    type: azure_openai
    # Endpoint deliberately absent, same as block 3's prompt: it carries
    # uniqueString(resourceGroup().id), so pinning it here would break this
    # file the first time the disposable resource group is rebuilt.
    azure_deployment: gpt-4.1-mini
  parameters:
    max_tokens: 200
    temperature: 0.2
sample:
  # evaluate_call.py reads `context` from this block and hands it to the
  # groundedness evaluator as the source the answer is checked against. A
  # prompt without it cannot be scored for groundedness at all.
  context: >
    A model deployment in Azure AI Foundry is created with a SKU that decides
    how it bills. Standard and GlobalStandard deployments bill per token
    consumed: no tokens, no charge, and the deployment costs nothing while
    idle. Provisioned deployments (ProvisionedManaged, GlobalProvisionedManaged
    and DataZoneProvisionedManaged) reserve throughput in provisioned units and
    bill for those units by the hour whether or not any request arrives. A
    provisioned deployment cannot be paused; the only way to stop it billing is
    to delete it.
  question: >
    I am building a learning environment I will use for a few minutes a day.
    Which deployment SKU should I choose, and what happens to the bill when I
    am not using it?
---

system:
You are answering questions about Azure AI Foundry.

Answer only from the material below. If the material does not cover part of
what was asked, say that it does not, rather than supplying the answer from
general knowledge. Do not add figures, percentages, discounts, free
allowances or billing intervals that do not appear in the material — an
invented number is the failure this instruction exists to prevent, and it is
the one that reads most like a real answer.

Here is some material:

{{context}}

user:
{{question}}
